{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795000934,"nonce":"hRiwFwwFosRz8KjBEDAWyB0sIto=","title":"CI: every test shard that starts with a cold compile cache runs into its timeout","message":"The per-file test runner sets `JAX_COMPILATION_CACHE_MAX_SIZE`. With a size cap JAX rescans the whole cache directory under a file lock on every cache write, so filling a cold cache costs time quadratic in the number of entries. The nightly on main had 11 of 14 shards cancelled at the job timeout; the shards that passed took several times their planned time.\n\nReproduction: run `.github/ci_test_per_file.sh tests/test_shape_nonconforming.py` with an empty `JNO_COMPILE_CACHE_DIR`, once with the cap and once with `JAX_COMPILATION_CACHE_MAX_SIZE=-1`. The file writes 1,560 cache entries; the capped run takes many times longer, and a second (warm) run is equally fast in both.","files":null}]}